dummy-x11 (1.0-10+crick) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Removed libXau/libXdmcp stubs: they were only needed by real libxcb's
    NEEDED, which is no longer in the package. The six remaining stub
    SONAMEs cover all browser imports.
  * gen-libxcb-stub: logging is now opt-in via DUMMY_X11_LOG env var.
    When the variable is empty or unset, no logging is performed (g_log
    stays NULL, log_entry/log_exit are no-ops). When set to a path, xcb_*
    calls are logged in append mode. Renamed from YABROWSER_XCB_LOG.
  * gen-libxcb-stub: has_error returns 0x0 (XCB_CONN_SUCCESS, no error)
    instead of using STATEFUL logic (0x1 once then 0x0). STATEFUL approach
    still resulted in 208 calls. New approach: always success +
    generate_id=0 (InvalidXID) + send_request=0 (error) — signals broken
    connection via invalid resources rather than connection-level errors.
  * gen-libxcb-stub: xcb_generate_id now returns 0 (InvalidXID) instead
    of 0xffffffff. Combined with has_error=0, this signals "no real X server"
    via invalid resource IDs rather than connection-level errors.
  * gen-libxcb-stub: xcb_send_request and xcb_send_request_with_fds now
    return 0 (error sequence). This makes failed X11 requests detectable
    by Chromium's ui/gfx/x code, potentially terminating the extension
    init loop early.
  * README.md completely rewritten to match current package state.
  * dummy-x11-report: removed libXau/libXdmcp from STUB_SONAMES.

  -- AI-agent <noreply@example.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Removed delegation to the real libxcb entirely. The logging stub no
    longer dlopen/dlsym the hidden libxcb-real.so.1 — it now returns a
    hardcoded value for the six functions the browser calls
    (xcb_connect, xcb_connect_to_display_with_auth_info,
    xcb_connection_has_error → 0x5, xcb_generate_id, xcb_flush,
    xcb_disconnect) and NULL for everything else. The real libxcb is
    removed from the package.
  * Removed the hidden real libxcb (debian/stubs/real/, installed to
    /usr/share/dummy-x11/hidden/) and the include-binaries entry that
    shipped it in the source package.
  * gen-libxcb-stub: deleted dlopen/dlsym, dlfcn.h, g_real_lib and the
    delegation wrapper; every non-overridden function now logs the call
    and returns NULL. Compiled without -ldl.
  * README.md, debian/control, dummy-x11-report and dummy-x11.conf
    updated to reflect that there is no real libxcb and no delegation.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix xcb_connection_has_error override: changed return value from 0x3
    (XCB_CONN_CLOSED_MEM_INSUFFICIENT — transient, browser retries 200+ times)
    to 0x5 (XCB_CONN_CLOSED_PARSE_ERR — permanent fatal). With 0x3 the browser
    never switched to Wayland despite 6 overridden functions. 0x5 is the same
    value real libxcb returns when no X server is available — forces immediate
    fallback to Wayland.
  * README.md and debian/control updated with corrected XCB enum names.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.none.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Override xcb_connect, xcb_connect_to_display_with_auth_info,
    xcb_connection_has_error, xcb_generate_id, xcb_flush, xcb_disconnect to
    return hardcoded values instead of delegating to real libxcb. Browser
    calls has_error 200+ times but doesn't switch to Wayland when only
    has_error is overridden. Now all called functions return stub values
    without touching real libxcb.
  * STUB_OVERRIDES expanded from 1 to 6 entries.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * xcb_connection_has_error overridden to return XCB_CONN_SERVER_UNAVAILABLE
    (0x3) instead of delegating to real libxcb (which returns
    XCB_CONN_WAITING_FOR_SETUP, 0x5). This forces Yandex Browser to fall back
    from X11 to Wayland.
  * Log file opened in append mode ("a") instead of truncate ("w") to prevent
    log entries from being lost when multiple processes use the stub.
  * README.md and dummy-x11-report updated with override documentation.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

